<task id="144" project="unified-access-control-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>C10 part 1 — secure records are owned by a NAMED, NON-DEFAULT, memberless owner team in a no-user Secure Record BU, for projects AND matters AND work assignments; provisioning refuses otherwise; existing secure rows migrated</title>
    <phase>Register-driven (authored 2026-09-30, session 27; defect C10 half 1; GitHub #967)</phase>
    <gate>startable. The RecordOwnershipResolver step waits for PR #1045 (word-add-in-r1) to merge to master and for master to be merged into this branch — that PR rewrites the same file.</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Authorization-boundary .cs change (tags bff-api, auth, security) plus an irreversible live-data migration of record ownership.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Security isolation boundary with high blast radius: changes who owns every secure record, generalizes provisioning to two more entity types, and includes a one-time ownership migration whose mistakes are silent disclosures.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Modifies ProvisionProjectEndpoint.cs, UnsecureProjectEndpoint.cs, DelegationRuleFilter.cs, RecordOwnershipResolver.cs, SECURE-PROJECT-ENVIRONMENT-SETUP.md and SecureBuRoleDepthAssertion*.cs — tasks 145 and 150 edit the same files and depend on this one; DelegationRuleFilter.cs is also a C4 hot file.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>none (RecordOwnershipResolver step gated on PR #1045 merge — see gate)</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, auth, security, dataverse, migration, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>8-12 hours</estimated-effort>
    <origin>Session 26 defect C10 (half 1) + session 27 owner round 2 item 6 ("add the Part 1 enforcement (named non-default owner team)"). Closes GitHub #967.</origin>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Stop relying on the Secure Record business unit's DEFAULT owner team staying empty. Own every secure project, matter and work assignment by a named, non-default owner team that provisioning resolves, proves memberless, and refuses to use otherwise; make the Secure Record BU a no-user BU and enforce that; give matters and work assignments the same secure/unsecure path projects have; and migrate the secure rows that already exist.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer on the Dataverse row-security isolation boundary. Expert in Dataverse ownership, business-unit depth, owner teams and the BFF ExternalAccess endpoints. Fail closed (ADR-003); verify every write by read-back.</role>

  <goal>After this task: (1) provisioning (for sprk_project, sprk_matter and sprk_workassignment) resolves the named non-default owner team in the Secure Record BU, asserts it has zero members and that no systemuser sits in the Secure Record BU, and refuses with a reason code otherwise; (2) every secure root row in dev is owned by that named team, none by the default team; (3) the unsecure path works for all three entity types; (4) RecordOwnershipResolver resolves the named team for children filed to a secure record; (5) registration refuses to place a user in the Secure Record BU; (6) the standing NFR-05 assertion targets the named team and fails on any member or any user in the BU; (7) the setup guide describes the named team; (8) #967 is closed with the outcome.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>🔴 TWO HOLES, ONE OF WHICH THE ORIGINAL DEFECT DID NOT NAME. Verified against source 2026-09-30.

HOLE 1 — THE DEFAULT TEAM (C10 half 1, #967). `ProvisionProjectEndpoint.cs:370-379` resolves the owner as the Secure Record BU's DEFAULT owner team (`_businessunitid_value eq {secureBuId} and isdefault eq true and teamtype eq 0`) and `:392-408` checks only the row count. Nothing checks membership. Dataverse maintains a default team's membership AUTOMATICALLY from each user's `businessunitid` and it cannot be curated, so an admin who moves any user into the Secure Record BU (a Change-BU, or `Services/Registration/RegistrationDataverseService.cs:355-376` given an operator-configured `BusinessUnitName` — `Api/RegistrationEndpoints.cs:319`) silently makes that user a member of the team that owns every secure record. The only detector is NFR-05 clause 2 (`tests/integration/auth/UnifiedAccessControl/SecureBuRoleDepthAssertion.cs:240-258`), which identifies the owner team as "the default team of the secure BU" (`SecureBuRoleDepthAssertionTests.cs:638`) and never runs in CI.

HOLE 2 — BU DEPTH, WHICH A NAMED TEAM ALONE DOES NOT CLOSE. A record owned by ANY team in the Secure Record BU has `owningbusinessunit` = that BU. A user placed in that BU whose ordinary roles carry Business Unit (Local) or Deep depth on sprk_project/sprk_matter/sprk_workassignment reads every secure record by DEPTH, whoever the owner team is. So moving ownership to a named team fixes the membership vector only. The owner's model — "a no-user BU where access is granted only explicitly" — therefore needs a second enforced invariant: ZERO systemusers (human or application) have `businessunitid` = the Secure Record BU.

HOLE 3 — MATTERS AND WORK ASSIGNMENTS ARE NEVER RE-OWNED. All three roots carry `sprk_issecure` (`ProvisionProjectEndpoint.cs:114-118`), but the only secure path is `/provision-project` (`ProvisionProjectEndpoint.cs:205-221`, mapped at `ExternalAccessEndpoints.cs:171-175`) and it reads and re-owns `sprk_projects` only (`:256-261`, `:609-616`). The reverse, `/unsecure-project`, is project-only too (`UnsecureProjectEndpoint.cs:46-47`, `:107-112`). A matter or work assignment flagged secure (today only possible via the MDA form) stays owned by its creator in an ordinary BU — not isolated at all — and, because `RecordContainerResolver.cs:244-266` fails closed on a secure record with no own `sprk_containerid`, every upload to it 409s. The DelegationRuleFilter cases are project-only too (`DelegationRuleFilter.cs:239-249`, `FromProjectId`).

HOLE 4 — CHILDREN FOLLOW THE DEFAULT TEAM. `RecordOwnershipResolver.ResolveFromTargetRecordAsync` (`Services/Dataverse/RecordOwnershipResolver.cs:220-242`) maps the target's `owningbusinessunit` to that BU's DEFAULT owner team. Once secure roots are owned by the named team, a child filed to a secure record would still be owned by the Secure BU's default team — the exact team this task retires. It has zero callers on this branch; PR #1045 (word-add-in-r1, OPEN) wires it for Office and edits the same file (`:233` there).

LIVE FACTS (session 27): dev has 1 secure project, provisioned, owned by the default team, with its own container; the owner role `Secure Record Owner` is assigned to the Secure BU default team; 0 documents are linked to any secure root.

What does NOT change here: the child re-own itself and the owner role's child privileges (C10 part 2 and task 145); the `sprk_issecure` field lock (task 150).</background>
