  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Re-verify every anchor in the background against current source and live dev (read-only): the owner role's team assignment, the default team's membership, systemusers in the Secure Record BU, `sharetopreviousowneronassign`, and every row with `sprk_issecure eq true` on the three roots with its owner and `sprk_containerid`. Record the census in the task note.</step>
    <step order="2">Grep for every other secure/unsecure path (writers of ownership on secure rows, readers that assume the default team — including `ProjectClosureEndpoint`, the e2e spec and the provisioning fixtures) and list them in the note; each one found is fixed in this task.</step>
    <step order="3">Implement named-team resolution plus the two runtime assertions (zero team members, zero BU users) in the provisioning path, before Step 5's assign, with new reason codes. Rewrite every statement that names the default team (class remarks `ProvisionProjectEndpoint.cs:13-25`, the `.WithDescription` at `:211-214`, the Step 3 comments `:360-369`, `:670`, `UnsecureProjectEndpoint.cs:30`).</step>
    <step order="4">Generalize provisioning and unsecure to sprk_matter and sprk_workassignment by extending the existing DTOs/handlers and the delegation-filter cases; per-entity entity sets and container naming come from one table, not three copies.</step>
    <step order="5">After PR #1045 is merged into this branch: make RecordOwnershipResolver return the named secure owner team when the target record's owning BU is the Secure Record BU; every other BU keeps its default team. Refuse (null) if the named team cannot be resolved — never the default team.</step>
    <step order="6">Guard `RegistrationDataverseService.CreateSystemUserAsync`: after `ResolveBusinessUnitIdAsync`, compare the resolved BU ID (not the name string) with the Secure Record BU ID resolved from `SecureRecord:BusinessUnitName` in the SAME target environment (`targetDataverseUrl`); a match is refused with an explicit error before the systemuser is created. An unreadable Secure BU lookup refuses (fail closed).</step>
    <step order="7">Retarget SecureBuRoleDepthAssertion: the owner team is the named team; clause 2 fails on ANY member; add the no-user-BU clause; clause 3 fails if the owner role is held by the Secure BU default team or any team but the named one. Seed each clause both ways in the unit tests.</step>
    <step order="8">Rewrite guide §4 (create the named owner team; assign the `Secure Record Owner` role to it; remove the role from the default team; zero-member and zero-user checks) and the §7 checklist; update the I-2 row of DATAVERSE-WRITE-PATH-ARCHITECTURE.md.</step>
    <step order="9" mode="prescriptive">Live cutover in dev, in this order: create the named team and assign the role (guide §4); run the migration dry run and record the plan; run with -Apply; verify read-back and share counts; remove the role from the default team; run the NFR-05 assertion and the §7 isolation probe by hand and record both outputs.</step>
    <step order="10">Build, unit + integration suites, publish-size measurement per CLAUDE.md §10.</step>
    <step order="11">Update TASK-INDEX.md: this task's status cell to `✅ [done]`; POML status to completed. Close #967 with the outcome. Document deviations in the task note.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>`organization.sharetopreviousowneronassign` is true in dev: STOP before any assign — the migration would share every secure row to the default team. Present the setting and a recommendation (turn it off, or strip the resulting shares) per CLAUDE.md §6.</trigger>
    <trigger>Any systemuser (human or application) currently sits in the Secure Record BU, or the default team has members: STOP. Report who, and do NOT move anyone — relocating users is an owner decision (owner directive: do not propose relocating users).</trigger>
    <trigger>The migration census finds a secure matter or work assignment that is NOT provisioned (user-owned, no own container) and has existing children or documents in a shared container: provisioning it does not retract content already in shared SPE storage. Report the rows and their content location and ask before provisioning them.</trigger>
    <trigger>Assigning to the named team fails with a privilege error naming anything other than a `Read` on a root table: the design says Read alone suffices; a different answer changes the design (task 145 owns the role's privileges).</trigger>
    <trigger>Any Dataverse relationship from sprk_project, sprk_matter or sprk_workassignment has Assign cascade = Cascade All/Active/UserOwned: the re-own reassigns children as a side effect, which overlaps C10 part 2. Record the cascade configuration and ask before migrating.</trigger>
    <trigger>OPEN OWNER QUESTION — the named team's name (compiled default for `SecureRecord:OwnerTeamName`). Before creating the live team in step 9, present the proposed name to the owner. Recommendation: `Secure Record Owners` (distinct from the BU's default team, which carries the BU's own name `Secure Record`, so the two can never be confused in MDA or in the census). The compiled default, the live team, the pinning test and guide §4 move together — the same fail-closed-lookup-key rule as `DefaultSecureBusinessUnitName` (`ProvisionProjectEndpoint.cs:122-133`).</trigger>
    <trigger>OPEN OWNER QUESTION — detection between provisioning calls. The runtime assertions fire only when something is provisioned; a Change-BU of a user into the Secure Record BU (which no BFF code can block without a plugin, D-1) exposes every EXISTING secure record until the next provisioning call or the next manual NFR-05 run. Recommendation: add a read-only ADR-036 `IScheduledJob` in the BFF (ADR-052 placement: BFF, schedule) that runs the zero-member and zero-BU-user census and logs a CRITICAL finding (no Dataverse writes, no CI involvement); needs a §10 placement statement. Ask the owner whether it is built in this task before step 3 is finished — do not silently leave the gap and do not build it unasked.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>`ProvisionProjectEndpoint.cs:370-416` (default-team resolution), `UnsecureProjectEndpoint.cs:87-281`, `RecordOwnershipResolver.cs:220-242`, `DelegationRuleFilter.cs:239-249`. Grep `SecureRecord:` over src/ finds only `SecureRecord:BusinessUnitName` (`ProvisionProjectEndpoint.cs:108`) and `SecureRecord:UnsecureOwnerUserId` (`UnsecureProjectEndpoint.cs:58`); no owner-team name key and no migration script under scripts/ (grep `Secure Record` over scripts/ = 0 hits).</existing>
    <extension>Yes for the endpoints, DTOs, filter cases, resolver and assertion — all extended in place, no new endpoint. The config key is an extension of the existing `SecureRecord:` section. Only the one-time migration script is new, because no existing script reassigns secure rows and a BFF endpoint for a one-time operator migration would be permanent surface for a one-shot need.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Any Change-BU of a user into the Secure Record BU grants that user Read on every secure project, matter and work assignment in MDA with no error (#967); secure matters and work assignments are not isolated at all and every upload to them returns 409; children filed to a secure record would be owned by the default team this task retires.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

